# d3-check project rule

When editing or adding code under **pyapps/d3-check** (Diablo III/IV macro, Battle.net, grid, D4):

1. **Prefer pycore.** Use `providor.common_imports` or direct `pycore.pyfoundations` / `pycore.pyutils` imports instead of new third-party libs or reimplementing. See `.cursor/skills/d3-check/SKILL.md` for typical pycore usage.

2. **D3/D4 constants and config → CONFIG.**
   - Literal constants (paths, resolutions, IDs, keywords, timeouts): put in **`providor.app_constants`**; other modules import from there.
   - Structured config (skill/macro/template, ConfigManager, grid): use **`config`** (unified_config, grid_config); literals still live in app_constants.

Do not add new literal constants in feature modules; add to `providor.app_constants` or the appropriate config module and import.

3. **Adding new standards (规范).** When the user asks to add a 规范, add it by priority: (1) `.cursor/rules` for project/file-scoped rules; (2) `.cursor/skills` for reusable skills with "When to Use"; (3) `pyapps/d3-check/AGENTS.md` for short sub-app instructions. This rule applies to the new 规范 as well—write it into rules, skills, or AGENTS.md accordingly.
